(requirement (id "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The profile's instruction set is RV64I plus the extensions M, A, F, D and C, plus Zicsr and Zifencei, plus Zicntr: 'G' is the defined abbreviation for the IMAFDZicsr_Zifencei base-and-extensions combination, and this profile is G plus C and Zicntr on the unprivileged side and Sstc on the privileged side.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-GC-COMPOSITION"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The extension dependency closure is complete under the pinned revision: D depends on F; F depends on Zicsr for control and status register access; and C decomposes as Zca always plus Zcd when D is present (Zcf exists only at RV32). Nothing in this profile is inferred from the letter 'G' alone.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZC") (locator "28.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-EXT-CLOSURE") (dependencies "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The privileged architecture is the pinned publication's: Machine-Level ISA Version 1.13 and Supervisor-Level ISA Version 1.13, under spec revision v20260120 — the same publication family as the unprivileged pin.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-PRIV-REVISION"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The profile implements machine, supervisor and user modes — the minimum a Linux-capable profile needs (M-mode firmware, S-mode kernel, U-mode userspace); the hypervisor extension is excluded, and every mode-dependent behaviour is tested in each supported mode (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-PRIV-MODES"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-SV39") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "Translation is Sv39: of the three paged virtual-memory schemes defined for SXLEN=64 (Sv39, Sv48, Sv57), the profile selects the minimal Linux-capable one — also the one the pinned SoC precedent implements (the FU540-C000's U54 supports Bare and Sv39). The U54's A/D behaviour (page faults instead of setting PTE A/D bits) is recorded as P4-SYSTEM.3's policy input, not as this profile's rule.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3–§11.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "SIFIVE-FU540-C000") (locator "§4.7")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-SV39") (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-IALIGN-16") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "With the C extension present, IALIGN is 16 — instructions start on any 16-bit boundary — while ILEN remains 32; no instruction-address-misaligned exception arises from C's 16-bit forms.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-IALIGN-16") (dependencies "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ZICNTR") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind state) (statement "The Zicntr base counters (cycle, time, instret) are included — explicitly beyond the G abbreviation — because a Linux-capable profile must offer the supervisor-mode time read; the counters' rate and progress semantics are the environment contract's to declare (P4-SYSTEM.5 and P4-SYSTEM.9), not this resolution's. Zihpm (hardware performance monitors) is not selected.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-ZICNTR") (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-SSTC") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind state) (statement "Sstc is included — the supervisor timer-compare register stimecmp, gated by menvcfg.STCE — so an S-mode kernel programs its own timer without an M-mode round trip.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-SSTC") (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-FP-DEFER") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "F and D are in the profile because the standard RV64G userspace ABI is LP64D, which requires the D extension; the model implements no floating point until the floating-point backend passes qualification (P4-SYSTEM.7), the CPU-SYSTEM gate verdict reads incomplete until then, and a Sail-versus-Spike floating-point comparison is one implementation twice (the SoftFloat shared ancestry), never independent numeric evidence.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-FP-DEFER") (dependencies "REQ-D-ABI"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ABI") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind environment) (statement "The toolchain ABI is LP64D — the standard RV64G ABI (ELFCLASS64 with EF_RISCV_FLOAT_ABI_DOUBLE, the hardware floating-point calling convention with ABI_FLEN=64); the toolchain is the host's clang/lld 21.1.8 with an rv64gc target (the existing guest-toolchain decision).") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-ABI"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-SBI") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind environment) (statement "The firmware contract for the Linux boot route is SBI 2.0: compatible M-mode firmware provides selected SBI services (timer, console, system reset, hart state management) before entering the S-mode kernel — real firmware, and a host-modelled SBI is a different contract, never silently substituted.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-SBI") (locator "Chapters 4–12")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-SBI"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-CSR-SET") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind state) (statement "The implemented CSR set is the committed minimum of 33: mhartid and misa; mstatus, mtvec, medeleg, mideleg, mie, mip, mscratch, mepc, mcause and mtval; menvcfg, mcounteren, mcycle and minstret; sstatus, stvec, sscratch, sepc, scause, stval, sie, sip and scounteren; satp; stimecmp; cycle, time and instret; and fflags, frm and fcsr. Per-CSR field semantics (WPRI/WARL/WLRL) belong to the privilege leaf (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-CSR") (locator "1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-CSR-SET") (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES") (dependencies "REQ-D-ZICNTR") (dependencies "REQ-D-SSTC"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-NO-PMP") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "PMP is excluded at v0: the privileged architecture's physical memory protection unit is optional, and the first boot contract does not require it; the decision is revisited by the board branch that needs it.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.7")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-NO-PMP"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-NO-H") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The hypervisor extension is excluded: the profile has one hart and no virtualization workload in the first Linux profile; H would arrive with a consumer, never ahead of one.") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-NO-H"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-RVWMO") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind memory) (statement "The memory consistency model is RVWMO: with the A extension in the profile the memory model is load-bearing even at one hart (the AMOs and their aq/rl annotations), and the multicore exposure of the weak model is MC-MULTICORE's, never smuggled in.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RVWMO") (locator "17.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-RVWMO"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The privileged instructions in scope are mret, sret, wfi and sfence.vma (the pinned privileged instruction listings); wfi's wake semantics belong to the interrupt/counter/wait leaf (P4-SYSTEM.5).") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-PRIV-INSNS") (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "This unit is a profile resolution: the selection is exact and citable, and the definition pipeline (encoding fragments, semantics, guests) has not started; the dossier declares the profile-resolution vehicle route, and the definition-pipeline gates refuse any encoding, state-census or guest-corpus document beside the declaration.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ROUTE-FLIP") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The definition pipeline has landed and the dossier declares the generated-definition vehicle route: the unit carries its encoding composition (the RV64I base plus Zicsr, Zicntr and the privileged-system fragment — (status partial) with six declared slots for M/A/F/D/C/Zifencei), the 33-CSR state document, the 62-guest corpus (the base mirror plus the mode matrix) and the 7-axis interaction matrix, and the generated mirrors (state_rv64gc.rs, definition_rv64gc.rs, guests_rv64gc.rs) are tracked because their canonical inputs are tracked in the same commit (decision_generated-mirror-needs-tracked-input).") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-ROUTE-FLIP") (dependencies "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind configuration) (statement "The scope block enumerates the RV64I base census (52 forms — the same enumeration and source as rv64i-lab-v0); each extension's instruction census lands with its encoding fragment in the evidence leaves (the RV32/64G listings and the privileged listings are the census references), and the declared scope grows only with them.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4–§1.1.8")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2–§3.1.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-G-LISTING") (locator "35.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification defines the options; the profile's selection among them is recorded here — a reference that selects otherwise is a smaller or different profile, not a defect in either.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-SCOPE-CENSUS"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ALU-IMM") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "ADDI adds the sign-extended 12-bit immediate to rs1, wrapping modulo 2^XLEN; overflow is ignored. SLTI and SLTIU compare rs1 against the sign-extended immediate, signed and unsigned respectively — SLTIU still sign-extends the immediate first and then compares unsigned. XORI, ORI and ANDI are bitwise against the sign-extended immediate.") (insns "addi") (insns "slti") (insns "sltiu") (insns "xori") (insns "ori") (insns "andi") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-ALU-IMM") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ALU-REG") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "ADD and SUB add and subtract modulo 2^XLEN; overflow is ignored and the result wraps. SLT and SLTU are signed and unsigned comparisons respectively, producing 0 or 1. XOR, OR and AND are bitwise.") (insns "add") (insns "sub") (insns "slt") (insns "sltu") (insns "xor") (insns "or") (insns "and") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-ALU-REG") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ECALL-EBREAK") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind event) (statement "ECALL and EBREAK cause a precise REQUESTED trap to the execution environment. With no privileged modes in this profile there is no guest handler, so both are reported to the harness as a typed environment-trap outcome and execution stops unless the harness contract says otherwise.") (insns "ecall") (insns "ebreak") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.8")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Exceptions/Traps/Interrupts (Requested Trap)")) (applicability included) (research_status partial) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification explicitly delegates this to the execution environment; this profile chose it, and a reference that chose differently is a profile difference, not a defect. OPEN: OQ-5 — the value of pc after a requested trap is not defined by the base ISA without a privileged mode, and this harness has not declared it. Owner: P0-PROFILE.4.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-ECALL-EBREAK"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-ENDIAN") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind memory) (statement "Little-endian. The specification delegates this to the EEI; endianness in RISC-V is byte-address invariant.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.6")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification explicitly delegates this to the execution environment; this profile chose it, and a reference that chose differently is a profile difference, not a defect.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-ENDIAN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-FENCE") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind memory) (statement "FENCE is decoded and must not trap. With one hart, no external devices and an in-order model, it has no observable effect. FENCE.TSO (fm=1000, pred=RW, succ=RW) is accepted and treated as FENCE RW,RW, which the specification states is correct. The remaining fm, pred and succ configurations are reserved, and the architecture SPECIFIES their behavior: base implementations shall treat all such reserved configurations as FENCE instructions (with fm = 0000) — they decode and execute as an ordinary FENCE, which under this profile has no observable effect. They do NOT fall under D-RESERVED-DECODE, and the rs1 and rd fields are ignored for forward compatibility, as the same section directs.") (insns "fence") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.7, Table 3 Fence mode encoding")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category implementation-defined) (detail "The specification explicitly delegates this to the execution environment; this profile chose it, and a reference that chose differently is a profile difference, not a defect.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-FENCE"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-JALR-LSB") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "JALR computes its target by adding the sign-extended 12-bit immediate to rs1 and then setting the least-significant bit of the result to zero.") (insns "jalr") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.5.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-JALR-LSB"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-LOAD-EXT") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "LW sign-extends its 32-bit result to 64 bits; LWU zero-extends it. LH/LB sign-extend and LHU/LBU zero-extend analogously. SD/SW/SH/SB store the low 64/32/16/8 bits of rs2.") (insns "lb") (insns "lh") (insns "lw") (insns "lbu") (insns "lhu") (insns "lwu") (insns "ld") (insns "sb") (insns "sh") (insns "sw") (insns "sd") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.3")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-LOAD-EXT") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN") (dependencies "REQ-D-ENDIAN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-LOAD-X0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "A load with rd = x0 must still raise any exceptions and cause any other side effects, even though the loaded value is discarded.") (insns "lb") (insns "lh") (insns "lw") (insns "lbu") (insns "lhu") (insns "lwu") (insns "ld") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.6")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-LOAD-X0"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-LUI-AUIPC") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "LUI places the 32-bit U-immediate in rd with the low 12 bits zeroed, sign-extended to 64 bits. AUIPC forms the same 32-bit offset, sign-extends it to 64 bits, and adds it to the address of the AUIPC instruction.") (insns "lui") (insns "auipc") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-LUI-AUIPC") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-NO-DELAY-SLOTS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "Control transfers have no architecturally visible delay slots.") (insns "jal") (insns "jalr") (insns "beq") (insns "bne") (insns "blt") (insns "bge") (insns "bltu") (insns "bgeu") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.5")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-NO-DELAY-SLOTS"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-SHAMT") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "SLLI/SRLI/SRAI take a 6-bit shift amount from the I-immediate; SLL/SRL/SRA use only the low 6 bits of rs2. SLLIW/SRLIW/SRAIW take 5 bits, and SLLW/SRLW/SRAW use rs2[4:0].") (insns "slli") (insns "srli") (insns "srai") (insns "sll") (insns "srl") (insns "sra") (insns "slliw") (insns "srliw") (insns "sraiw") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2.1, §3.1.2.2")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-SHAMT") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-WSUFFIX") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The *W instructions ignore the upper 32 bits of their inputs, produce a 32-bit signed result, and sign-extend it to 64 bits — bits XLEN-1 through 31 are equal. Overflow is ignored.") (insns "addiw") (insns "slliw") (insns "srliw") (insns "sraiw") (insns "addw") (insns "subw") (insns "sllw") (insns "srlw") (insns "sraw") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2, §3.1.2.1, §3.1.2.2")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-WSUFFIX") (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-D-XLEN") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind state) (statement "XLEN = 64. The integer registers and the supported user address space are 64 bits.") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states this outright; the model has no latitude.")) (risk low) (obligation_ids "OB-XLEN"))
(requirement (id "REQ-GC-CSR-ACCESS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The Zicsr instructions atomically read and write the addressed CSR under the uniform permission model: csrrw swaps, csrrs sets bits, csrrc clears bits, and the immediate forms use the zero-extended 5-bit uimm; csrrw/csrrwi with rd=x0 do not read the CSR; csrrs/csrrc with rs1=x0 and csrrsi/csrrci with uimm=0 do not write it. An access below the address's privilege level, a write to a read-only address, a counter read gated off by mcounteren (and scounteren in U), an stimecmp access below M with mcounteren.TM=0 or menvcfg.STCE=0, and a satp access in S with mstatus.TVM=1 each raise an illegal-instruction exception.") (insns "csrrw") (insns "csrrs") (insns "csrrc") (insns "csrrwi") (insns "csrrsi") (insns "csrrci") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICSR") (locator "5.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-CSR") (locator "1.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.11")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.1.5")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The specification states the swap/set/clear rules and the no-read/no-write disciplines outright; the permission model is §1.1.1's address map plus the named gates.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-GC-CSR-ACCESS"))
(requirement (id "REQ-GC-PRIV-INSNS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The privileged system instructions behave per mode: mret/sret execute in their mode or higher and raise illegal-instruction below it (sret also raises in S when mstatus.TSR=1); wfi executes as a no-op when legal (the specification's own latitude), raises illegal-instruction in U (S is present), and in S when mstatus.TW=1; sfence.vma raises illegal-instruction in U and in S with mstatus.TVM=1, and its invalidation effect is a stated no-op at this stage (no translation caches are modelled; Sv39 is P4-SYSTEM.3). xRET pops the two-level privilege stack (xIE<-xPIE, mode<-xPP, xPIE<-1, xPP<-U), clears MPRV when the target is not M, and sets pc<-xepc.") (insns "mret") (insns "sret") (insns "wfi") (insns "sfence.vma") (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.6.6")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.2.1")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The chapters state the legality matrix outright; the wfi no-op and the latitudes' resolution are laboratory choices, recorded in definitions/riscv/system.sem.sexp.")) (risk high) (obligation_ids "OB-GC-PRIV-INSNS"))
(requirement (id "REQ-GC-COUNTERS") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (kind instruction) (statement "The Zicntr counter reads rdcycle/rdtime/rdinstret read the cycle/time/instret values into rd; they are csrrs specializations (rs1=x0, the counter's address) and obey the counter-enable gates: below M the read is legal only with the mcounteren bit, and in U additionally the scounteren bit; the counters' rate and progress are the environment contract's (P4-SYSTEM.5/.9).") (insns "rdcycle") (insns "rdtime") (insns "rdinstret") (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.11")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.1.5")) (applicability included) (research_status resolved) (implementation_status planned) (source_semantics (category defined) (detail "The chapter defines the reads; the gating is the machine/supervisor chapters'; progress is explicitly deferred.")) (risk medium) (obligation_ids "OB-GC-COUNTERS"))
